{"availability":"available","full":"brass-cz/brass","name":"brass","description":"A statically and flexibly type-inferred scripting language with just-in-time compilation","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":55,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-27T13:12:21Z","updated":"2026-08-26T05:33:31Z","license":"MPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://brass-cz.org","topics":["jit-compiler","programming-language","type-inference"],"demo":"https://brass-cz.org/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.359Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.359Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.359Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.359Z","stars":55,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Brass is a statically typed, structurally typed scripting language with flexible type inference. Its .cz source extension comes from copper and zinc, the two metals that make up brass. A Brass program runs like a script, but every function is fully type-checked just before it executes, and most types are inferred rather than written. A just-in-time compiler runs the program at native speed; an interpreter backs the REPL and WebAssembly."],"features":["Type inference everywhere. Flexible inference means most code needs","no annotations; types are resolved per function, just before it runs.","Records and sum types under one type keyword. Methods are implemented","with fun T.m(...): a first self parameter makes an instance method, otherwise it is static; Self refers to the type.","Structural subtyping with interface contracts. type B: A requires B to"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brass-cz/brass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6d2e888c64582b45d3f0778abe5ee6595e0017814b9e8bddfd89f4e40b84614b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.520Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:11.520Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Brass is a statically typed, structurally typed scri